#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:3
msgid "RDMA Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:15
msgid "1. Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:18
msgid "1-1. What is RDMA controller?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:20
msgid ""
"RDMA controller allows user to limit RDMA/IB specific resources that a given "
"set of processes can use. These processes are grouped using RDMA controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:23
msgid ""
"RDMA controller defines two resources which can be limited for processes of "
"a cgroup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:27
msgid "1-2. Why RDMA controller needed?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:29
msgid ""
"Currently user space applications can easily take away all the rdma verb "
"specific resources such as AH, CQ, QP, MR etc. Due to which other "
"applications in other cgroup or kernel space ULPs may not even get chance to "
"allocate any rdma resources. This can lead to service unavailability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:34
msgid ""
"Therefore RDMA controller is needed through which resource consumption of "
"processes can be limited. Through this controller different rdma resources "
"can be accounted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:39
msgid "1-3. How is RDMA controller implemented?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:41
msgid ""
"RDMA cgroup allows limit configuration of resources. Rdma cgroup maintains "
"resource accounting per cgroup, per device using resource pool structure. "
"Each such resource pool is limited up to 64 resources in given resource pool "
"by rdma cgroup, which can be extended later if required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:46
msgid ""
"This resource pool object is linked to the cgroup css. Typically there are 0 "
"to 4 resource pool instances per cgroup, per device in most use cases. But "
"nothing limits to have it more. At present hundreds of RDMA devices per "
"single cgroup may not be handled optimally, however there is no known use "
"case or requirement for such configuration either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:52
msgid ""
"Since RDMA resources can be allocated from any process and can be freed by "
"any of the child processes which shares the address space, rdma resources "
"are always owned by the creator cgroup css. This allows process migration "
"from one to other cgroup without major complexity of transferring resource "
"ownership; because such ownership is not really present due to shared nature "
"of rdma resources. Linking resources around css also ensures that cgroups "
"can be deleted after processes migrated. This allow progress migration as "
"well with active resources, even though that is not a primary use case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:61
msgid ""
"Whenever RDMA resource charging occurs, owner rdma cgroup is returned to the "
"caller. Same rdma cgroup should be passed while uncharging the resource. "
"This also allows process migrated with active RDMA resource to charge to new "
"owner cgroup for new resource. It also allows to uncharge resource of a "
"process from previously charged cgroup which is migrated to new cgroup, even "
"though that is not a primary use case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:68
msgid ""
"Resource pool object is created in following situations. (a) User sets the "
"limit and no previous resource pool exist for the device of interest for the "
"cgroup. (b) No resource limits were configured, but IB/RDMA stack tries to "
"charge the resource. So that it correctly uncharge them when applications "
"are running without limits and later on when limits are enforced during "
"uncharging, otherwise usage count will drop to negative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:76
msgid ""
"Resource pool is destroyed if all the resource limits are set to max and it "
"is the last resource getting deallocated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:79
msgid ""
"User should set all the limit to max value if it intents to remove/"
"unconfigure the resource pool for a particular device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:82
msgid ""
"IB stack honors limits enforced by the rdma controller. When application "
"query about maximum resource limits of IB device, it returns minimum of what "
"is configured by user for a given cgroup and what is supported by IB device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/cgroup-v1/rdma.rst:87
msgid "Following resources can be accounted by rdma controller."
msgstr ""

